-- sort.cub — Remark 9.15 “the declaration”, in §9 “Ordering — what counting discards” of the earlier paper
-- "Respecting Equality", cited in this repository before 2026-11-11 (docs/index.html of the earlier
-- repository avikj/math, last changed 8 Oct 2026, sha256 984fafe88eb6…; no copy is in this repository);
-- Definition 9.6 “merge” and Theorem 9.2 “the fibre is the relabellings” below are that section's too. The repository's copy of the paper
-- (docs/Hyperactive_Final_Paper.pdf, 11 Nov 2026, sha256 e8f358b4cd2c…) does not contain it. The declaration
-- Σ[B] (B a rearrangement of X) × Sorted B over a type with a
-- total order, posed with the identities a finite bag has and normalized: the elimination of X,
-- whose ∪ branch is merge. A bag is the free commutative monoid on the type (∪ with units,
-- associativity and commutativity as path constructors); a rearrangement is equality of
-- multiplicities, counted with the equality the order decides (x = y when x ≤ y and y ≤ x);
-- Sorted is Definition 9.6 “merge”'s. The elements are only ever arguments of the comparator.
-- Loaded after lib/std.cub.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- a type with a total order
TotalOrder : {A : Type} → (A → A → Bool) → Type
TotalOrder le =
  ((x : A) → isTrue (le x x)) ×
  ((x y : A) → le x y ≡ false → isTrue (le y x)) ×
  ((x y z : A) → isTrue (le x y) → isTrue (le y z) → isTrue (le x z)) ×
  ((x y : A) → isTrue (le x y) → isTrue (le y x) → x ≡ y)
